SYDO reference instance: sydo_512f

Directory layout:

  Makefile
    Builds the NGCC SIG_AlgorithmInstance wrapper, KAT generator, and benchmark.
  SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c/.h
    NGCC signature API wrapper for this instance.
  src/
    ISO C SYDO reference implementation sources.
  lib/
    NGCC auxiliary functions, DRNG, and BLAKE2 reference sources.
  test/
    Local KAT and benchmark drivers.

Environment requirements:

- POSIX-like environment with `make`.
- ISO C compiler with C11 support.
- `taskset` from util-linux is recommended for benchmark pinning on Linux.

Build:

  make clean
  make CC=gcc

Run benchmark on one CPU core:

  taskset -c 0 ./bench

The default benchmark build uses the x86/x86-64 TSC reader for real
`*_cycles` and `*_mcycles` on x86/x86-64 machines. This is benchmark-only code
in `test/bench.c`; it is not used by the SYDO reference algorithm
implementation.

Portable ISO C benchmark fallback:

Use this fallback when building in a pure ISO C environment or on a platform
without x86 TSC. It uses `clock()` for elapsed time and does not use
instruction-set-specific cycle counters. In this mode `*_cycles` and
`*_mcycles` are reported as 0 unless `BENCH_CPU_HZ` is supplied at compile
time. `BENCH_CPU_HZ` is the CPU frequency in Hz and must be replaced with the
measured or otherwise confirmed frequency of the benchmark machine, for example:

  make clean
  make CC=gcc CPPFLAGS_EXTRA="-DBENCH_PORTABLE_ISO_C -DBENCH_CPU_HZ=CPU_FREQUENCY_HZ"
  taskset -c 0 ./bench

For x86/x86-64 benchmark runs with real cycle counts, use the default build:

  make clean
  make CC=gcc
  taskset -c 0 ./bench

Generate test vectors:

  ./kat_sig

The KAT file is written to:

  output/KAT_SIG_sydo_512f.txt

Clean generated files:

  make clean

Copyright and third-party notices are listed in ../NOTICE.
